  "item": [
    {
      "name": "[ASR] Get Languages",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "header": [],
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{base_url}}/asr/v3/languages",
          "host": [
            "{{base_url}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "asr",
            "v3",
            "languages"
          ]
        },
        "description": "## Overview\n\nRetrieves the list of languages supported by the GhanaNLP Automatic Speech Recognition (ASR) API. Use this endpoint to discover which language codes are available before making a transcription request.\n\n## Authentication\n\nThis request requires an API key. Pass it using the `{{api_key}}` variable, which should be set in your active environment.\n\n## Request\n\n**Method:** GET\n\nNo request body or query parameters are required.\n\n## Response\n\nReturns a list of supported ASR languages. Each language entry typically includes:\n\n- **Language name** – The human-readable name of the language (e.g., Twi, Ga, Dagbani, Ewe)\n- **Language code** – The short code used when making transcription requests (e.g., `tw`, `gaa`, `dag`, `ee`)\n\n### Known Supported Languages\n\n| Language | Code  |\n|----------|-------|\n| Twi      | `tw`  |\n| Ga       | `gaa` |\n| Dagbani  | `dag` |\n| Ewe      | `ee`  |\n\n## Notes\n\n- Use the language codes returned by this endpoint as the `language` query parameter in the **[ASR] Transcribe Twi Audio** request.\n- This endpoint is part of the [GhanaNLP / Khaya AI](https://translation.ghananlp.org) platform, which provides NLP services for Ghanaian and African languages."
      },
